{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>A sea wind.</b> A westerly wind." "<b>The Sea of Reeds.</b> I say that the Sea of Reeds was partly in the west, opposite the entire southern coast, and also in the east of the land of Israel — therefore a sea wind drove the locusts into the Sea of Reeds opposite it. And so we find regarding boundaries that it extends to the east, as it is said: ״מִיַּם סוּף וְעַד יָם פְּלִשְׁתִּים״ (further on, 23:31) — from east to west, for the sea of the Philistines was in the west, as is said of the Philistines: ״יוֹשְׁבֵי חֶבֶל הַיָּם גּוֹי כְּרֵתִים״ (Zephaniah 2)." "<b>Not one locust remained.</b> Even the salted ones that they had salted from them."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:23.831408799Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}